## 🧪 Roteiro de Aula (Passo a passo)

### 1) Imports e Configuração
```python
import pandas as pd
import numpy as np
import ast
from datetime import datetime
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt

pd.set_option("display.max_columns", 100)
pd.set_option("display.width", 120)
np.random.seed(42)
plt.rcParams.update({"figure.figsize": (8, 5)})
```

### 2) Carregamento do CSV e Diagnóstico Inicial
```python
csv_path = "tmdb_5000_movies.csv"
df = pd.read_csv(csv_path)

df.head()
df.info()
df.describe().T
df.isna().sum().sort_values(ascending=False).head(20)
```

### 3) Limpeza e Feature Engineering
```python
if "release_date" in df.columns:
    df["release_date"] = pd.to_datetime(df["release_date"], errors="coerce")
    df["release_year"] = df["release_date"].dt.year

for c in ["budget", "revenue", "runtime", "vote_average", "vote_count", "popularity"]:
    if c in df.columns:
        df[c] = pd.to_numeric(df[c], errors="coerce")

if {"budget", "revenue"}.issubset(df.columns):
    df["profit"] = df["revenue"] - df["budget"]
    df["roi"] = np.where(df["budget"] > 0, (df["revenue"] - df["budget"]) / df["budget"], np.nan)

for c in ["budget", "revenue"]:
    if c in df:
        mu, sigma = df[c].mean(), df[c].std(ddof=0)
        df[f"{c}_z"] = (df[c] - mu) / sigma
```

---

### 4) Análises Descritivas e Agrupamentos
```python
if {"revenue", "title"}.issubset(df.columns):
    top_rev = df.sort_values("revenue", ascending=False).head(10)[["title", "revenue", "budget", "profit", "roi"]]
    display(top_rev)

if "release_year" in df.columns:
    releases_by_year = df["release_year"].value_counts().sort_index()
